A_612 - For people who appreciate the chocolate flavor, I recommend gradually switching from drinking coffee to drinking liquid chocolate. Simply put, when sugar is also present in the liquid, bitter cocoa melts and mixes. It is the presence of sugar that makes bitter cocoa melt, it is not the temperature of the liquid as many might think. The bitter cocoa melts and becomes drinkable even in cold water, the important thing is that there is enough sugar. This suggestion of mine arises from the fact that coffee, being roasted, is bad for the stomach, while cocoa, being bitter but not toasted, does not have this harmful effect on the stomach.